WEBVTT

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:04.333
This is Sanket Tambare's website, read aloud.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:11.300
An engineer from Pune who runs ultras, climbs Sahyadri forts, and writes in English and Marathi.

00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:14.467
Its first line: “Don't read about me. Ask me.”

00:00:16.833 --> 00:00:22.833
Each bar is one month of his life since 2018. Grey is the feed. Colour is everything else.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:26.900
Loud, then quiet, then loud again. That's the whole story.

00:00:28.867 --> 00:00:36.300
And it listens. Ask out loud and, like Wispr Flow, it strikes out the ums, then answers from his archive.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.967
If it doesn't know, it says so.

00:00:40.933 --> 00:00:48.467
Kilometre 5: the feed. In college he ran social media, and posted almost daily: 997 micro-posts.

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:55.500
In 2020 he built a social network. Then he read Permanent Record, and started writing about privacy.

00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:04.433
Kilometre 10: the quiet years. A job, a policy fellowship, and just 24 essays in four years.

00:01:04.733 --> 00:01:06.800
The site calls it mistake №1.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:15.067
Kilometre 15. His first 10K, in 2023, took 1:26:40.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:21.267
His first half marathon: 2:45:52. Eighteen months later: 1:59:57.

00:01:21.533 --> 00:01:24.533
26 races since, up to 50 km.

00:01:26.533 --> 00:01:31.700
Kilometre 21: the ridges. 20 treks, each a peak as tall as the hours on foot.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.733
The tallest: Panhala to Pawankhind. 22 hours, through the night.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.633
Kilometre 30: the wall. Six mistakes, in his own words.

00:01:42.967 --> 00:01:48.867
“I had no energy to run, I had given up but with Nikhil, I managed to finish well!”

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:54.267
“But, you have to endure, adjust and make sure you finish off what you started.”

00:01:56.267 --> 00:02:00.900
Kilometre 35. In 2025, he left Instagram.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:08.033
This year he promised 100 posts. He's at 79, with 7.5× last year's words.

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:15.200
Kilometre 38: flow. 20 projects this year, almost all built alone.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:22.667
A campaign to save Pune's last wild hill. Data stories. A school portal for an NGO in the Satpuda.

00:02:24.633 --> 00:02:30.333
Kilometre 40: how he thinks. An early sentence, beside its closest match from this year.

00:02:30.633 --> 00:02:33.467
And a shelf of 52 books, in two languages.

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:40.100
The finish. In June he wrote: “I just start and the words just appear!”

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:45.900
That's Wispr Flow in one line. So the site ends with three campaigns he'd run for Flow in India.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:54.967
Every number here was read live from his archive. Change it in the admin dashboard, and the site and this film follow.

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:58.367
Don't read about him. Ask him — out loud.
